(1) Re: starting as an archeologist.  A few versions back, I had a very good 
run of A-starts where I would dig a trapdoor, fall through, and half the time
land in a shop.  Maybe it was just luck; hasn't happened at all, lately.

(2) Re: idea for a new special level.  Well, not a special level, just a new 
kind of shop--a junkyard.  It would appear only fairly deep; prices would be 
very low; most but not necessarily all goods would be damaged (cursed, out of
charges, or whatever is appropriate "damage" in a given class of items)--ideal 
for the do-it-your-selfer who has loads of holy water, scrolls of charging, 
and so on.  Service would of course be surly, and there'd likely be one or 
more junkyard dogs (J's that aren't jabberwocks) to watch out for.

(3) Re: unusual messages.  The other day, playing a telepathic rogue with 
automatic searching, wearing a blindfold in hell, I was walking along 
peacefully when I read "You discover a kobold pretending to be a statue"
or words to that effect ("disguised as," maybe?). Sho'nuff, that's what it
was.  Is this message more common if you are, say, an elf?  


